[ty] Contextualize generator expression yields

`generator_types` does a lot of work to handle unions, intersections, etc. None of this is done for `Iterable`, so we won't support a type context of e.g. `Iterable[int] | None`.

I think the more correct general approach for this whole `yield_tcx` block is actually to construct the synthetic type `GeneratorType[T,  Any, Any]` (representing the concrete type of the generator) and try to constraint-set-assign that to the type context (with `T` inferable), and solve for `T`. That should handle all the cases via assignability. (For an async generator it would need to be an `AsyncGeneratorType` instead.) We shouldn't be just special-casing certain types here.

(Even `generator_types` itself has a TODO comment up top explaining that it itself is a big pile of special-casing that shouldn't exist.)

